== AC-7.5 regression: file tree double click and search result double click ==
The jump lane does not modify the file-tree/search code (frozen contract boundary);
these are the existing lane suites, rebuilt and run from the current working tree.

--- vedit-filetree-tests (standalone lane build: tree.dblclick.* / tree.activate.*) ---
[vedit-filetree-tests-exit=0]
CHECK tree.dblclick.rect-visible ok=1
CHECK tree.dblclick.view-signal ok=1 detail="1"
CHECK tree.dblclick.folder-expands ok=1
CHECK tree.dblclick.folder-does-not-open ok=1
CHECK tree.dblclick.file-rect ok=1
CHECK tree.dblclick.file-opens ok=1 detail="1"
CHECK tree.dblclick.file-path ok=1 detail="/vedit-build/filetree-testdata/tree/top.v"
CHECK tree.activate.file-opens ok=1
FILETREE-TESTS checks=111 failures=0

--- vedit-workspace-search-selftest (standalone lane build: jump.click.* is the row click -> jump path) ---
[vedit-workspace-search-selftest-exit=0]
CHECK jump.hit-row-exists PASS
CHECK jump.row-visible PASS
CHECK jump.click.recorded PASS
CHECK jump.click.file PASS
CHECK jump.click.line PASS
CHECK jump.click.column PASS
CHECK jump.file-row.no-jump PASS
CHECK jump.activate PASS
CHECK jump.demo.opened PASS
CHECK jump.demo.line PASS

NOTE: in the ROOT (product) build the same search selftest passes every check including
jump.click.* but then crashes on ApplicationShell destruction (SIGSEGV) - a shell/editor
teardown defect in the lane currently being rewritten; see root-build-status.log item 5.
